================================================================================
Fix: analytics banner keeps saying "enable it in Settings" after enabling it
================================================================================

Context
-------

User report: ticked Settings -> Global -> "Compute large-graph metrics on
Databricks", saved, went to Analytics, and the amber over-limit banner still
ended with "...or enable Compute large-graph metrics on Databricks in
Settings -> Global (admin only)".

The setting was stored correctly. Read directly from the live Lakebase registry
(benoit_cayla / ontobricks_demo, Postgres schema ontobricks_demo,
global_config JSONB): `analytics_job_enabled = True`, updated_at
2026-07-31 05:44:44Z — 62 seconds before the report. The deployed app already
carried yesterday's `_jobBlockedReason` work, so the code was current too.

Root cause: the banner reads job availability from `/dtwin/sync/stats`
(`analytics_job_available` + `analytics_job_blocked_reason`), and the Analytics
page fetches it *without* `refresh=true` — deliberately, because the aggregate
counts behind it are expensive on a 7.6M-triple graph. That payload is cached on
the domain session for `_TS_STATS_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS` (300s), and the cache
validity check added yesterday only tests that the fields are *present*, not
that they still agree with the stored toggle. Nothing invalidated the section
when an admin flipped the setting, so for up to five minutes the page served the
pre-change answer.

That is exactly the branch the banner takes when the toggle reads as off, which
is why an admin who had just enabled it was told to go and enable it — and why
it was indistinguishable from the save having failed.

Changes
-------

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   New `clear_ts_cache(section)`: drops one cached triplestore section and
   persists the session, leaving the other sections (`status`, `dt_existence`)
   alone. The TTL cannot cover a setting that changes what a section reports.

2. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   `save_analytics_job_enabled_result` now drops the cached `stats` section
   after a successful write, so the next Analytics load recomputes availability.
   Best-effort: the value is already committed, so a failure to invalidate is
   logged rather than turned into a 500.

3. tests/units/settings/test_analytics_toggle_invalidates_stats.py (new, 10 tests)
   `clear_ts_cache` round-trip, section isolation, absent-section no-op and
   persistence; save-path invalidation for both on and off; unrelated sections
   preserved; invalidation failure does not fail the save; nothing dropped when
   the write itself failed; plus a guard on the TTL premise.

Not changed
-----------

`/dtwin/metrics/compute` resolves job availability live, so an actual run always
used the current setting — only the banner was stale.

Modified files
--------------
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
- src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
- tests/units/settings/test_analytics_toggle_invalidates_stats.py (new)
- changelogs/v0.7.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-07-31.log (new)

Tests: pytest -q -m "not scenario" -> 3783 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected
in 28.48s.

